WEBVTT

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.875
Miss Umako...

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.000
Don't come near me!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.417
These soaps sure are great.

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:39.750
Something came over me before.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.042
Not at all. Miss, run away with me!

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.875
I'm flattered that you would ask me.

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:49.000
But I cannot do anything.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.917
So what about the count's power?

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:55.917
<i>I want to hold Master's hands, too.</i>

00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:59.083
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:01.667
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:05.375
<i>A bell in my heart is ringing</i>

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.000
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:16.917
<i>It all started way back then </i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:22.500
<i>Ever since before we were born</i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.750
<i>you were destined to appear out of nowhere,</i>

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.750
<i>right before my eyes,</i>

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.542
<i>I'm sure of it</i>

00:01:33.542 --> 00:01:39.208
<i>My wishes and ambitions and daydreams</i>

00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:44.875
<i>take me to an unknown level and knock on a door</i>

00:01:44.875 --> 00:01:51.083
<i>You give me the key and the future</i>
<i>I need to take flight (with your wings)</i>

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.042
<i>There's no stopping it</i>

00:01:57.042 --> 00:02:02.708
<i>It's a sign, rung by an angel, saying "I love you"</i>

00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.583
<i>Can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.917
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:02:07.917 --> 00:02:13.333
<i>A bell in my heart that I've </i>
<i>never heard before is ringing</i>

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:22.458
<i>But even so, you don't suspect a thing</i>

00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:28.542
Culture.

00:02:28.542 --> 00:02:33.583
The Age of Exploration was also
the start of a new cultural exchange.

00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:36.792
The Europeans learned of the
various other peoples and cultures

00:02:36.792 --> 00:02:38.708
that existed in the world.

00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:42.500
Even as they regarded the Native
American people to be uncivilized,

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.667
it is said that they were captivated

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.125
by the level of their culture
and abundance of their riches.

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:52.000
Yes, just as a certain Angeloid
calls humans "Downers,"

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.833
which is to say, earthbound bugs,
while being fascinated by them.

00:02:55.833 --> 00:03:01.458
Oh, my, do you mean Nymph?
Or could that be Ikaros?

00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:03.083
Mikako...

00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:11.833
It is somewhat curious, huh?

00:03:11.833 --> 00:03:12.917
Dog,

00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:15.583
are you in on this, as well?

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:19.583
"Where the Melodious Words Of an Angel Go"

00:03:20.875 --> 00:03:21.500
"42nd Joint Culture Festival"

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.250
It's culture festival time.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.750
Culture festival?

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.375
It's kind of like a festival
just for the school.

00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.750
The classes and clubs put up booths,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.750
and hold performances up on the stage.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.167
Master, are you going
to be taking part, as well?

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.833
Nah, it's too big a pain.

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.500
I'm free to participate or not
in the class activity, so I passed.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:50.125
And I'm not in any of the clubs.

00:03:51.125 --> 00:03:52.792
We've been waiting for you, Tomoki.

00:03:52.792 --> 00:03:55.250
The New World Discovery
Club has settled on its performance

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.333
This is it! We're now
looking for acclaimed pilots.

00:03:58.333 --> 00:03:59.292
No, thanks!

00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:01.833
Don't say that. It is
an honor to be selected

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:03.792
from the many members
of the New World Discover Club.

00:04:03.792 --> 00:04:07.667
Just a minute!
When did I ever join your club?!

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.625
According to the student council rolls,

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:11.958
you are being treated as a club member.

00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:14.333
It's a conspiracy! Someone is hatching a plot!

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.292
Oh...

00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:18.125
...what have we here?

00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:20.625
What a shabby looking gateway.

00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:22.792
Look there, Yoshitsune,

00:04:22.792 --> 00:04:26.708
the poor people are calling this
a full-fledged culture festival.

00:04:26.708 --> 00:04:29.583
I wonder if they even
know the meaning of "culture."

00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:33.042
There they are!
The guys from the private school!

00:04:33.042 --> 00:04:34.792
Who are those guys?

00:04:34.792 --> 00:04:37.625
Students from the nearby
Sorami Private Academy.

00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:40.500
As remote as we are,
there aren't very many students,

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.792
so each year, we hold
our culture festivals together.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.917
They do not seem to get along.

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:49.917
Sparks are flying.

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:55.833
Look, Tsukino, they're making
flowers out of cardboard.

00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:57.917
I'm concerned that if these
apes haven't even mastered fire yet,

00:04:57.917 --> 00:05:00.708
how are they going to express any culture?

00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:01.667
What was that?!

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.958
Then what are you guys
doing at this year's culture festival?!

00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:06.167
--I'll just bet it's something pretentious and dull!

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:09.458
--Well, we're putting on...
--I'll just bet it's something pretentious and dull!

00:05:10.292 --> 00:05:12.458
...a <i>furuoke </i>concert.

00:05:13.417 --> 00:05:16.083
Did you hear that, Sohara?!
These guys are such idiots!

00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:17.167
What?

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.875
I mean, this is a culture festival,

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.417
and they're going to be taking baths!

00:05:20.417 --> 00:05:24.875
Just go to a bathhouse,
you dumb dummies!

00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:26.958
That's a <i>furo-oke</i>.
[<i>furo-oke: </i>"bathtub"]

00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:30.958
"<i>Furuoke</i>" means "full orchestra," Tomo.

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:32.708
He doesn't even know
what <i>furuoke </i>means.

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:35.125
You really have to
feel sorry for poor people.

00:05:35.125 --> 00:05:37.583
Let's head back, everyone.

00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:40.917
If we stay here,
the apes will rub off on us.

00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:44.917
Geez, Tomo, thanks to you,
they made us sound extra foolish!

00:05:44.917 --> 00:05:46.125
Damn!

00:05:46.125 --> 00:05:48.000
Sohara, if that's how they want it,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.625
let's do something for
the culture festival, too.

00:05:49.625 --> 00:05:51.500
Something like what?

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.958
Well, uh...

00:05:55.542 --> 00:05:59.375
I am a bit offended as well.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:06.167
As Student Council Chairman,
I can't very well back down from this.

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.250
If they're going to
come at us with music,

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.958
then we'll take them
on with music, as well.

00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:13.875
What do you say to a band concert?

00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:16.208
B-Band concert?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.083
"Music Room"

00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:22.750
<i>How is she getting that kind</i>
<i>of sound out of a tambourine?</i>

00:06:29.458 --> 00:06:30.458
<i>No way.</i>

00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:34.250
<i>There's absolutely no way we can</i>
<i>form a band with us as members.</i>

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.667
<i>But then, we've got</i>
<i>no other choice, do we?</i>

00:06:43.375 --> 00:06:49.875
<i>Master's hands... How do I get</i>
<i>Master to hold my hands?</i>

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.083
<i>I know. I will work really hard,</i>

00:06:52.083 --> 00:06:55.917
<i>until I get Master to give</i>
<i>me his praise, and then surely...</i>

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.542
That's awesome, Nymph!

00:07:09.542 --> 00:07:11.917
Amazing, Nymph!

00:07:11.917 --> 00:07:15.042
Who knew that you
had such a special talent?

00:07:15.042 --> 00:07:18.250
I specialize in machines and such, so...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.333
If we can have her back us
up on the harder parts of our song,

00:07:21.333 --> 00:07:23.667
then maybe the band won't sound
like it was just thrown together.

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:29.583
All right, great! We'll show
those private school guys!

00:07:29.583 --> 00:07:32.958
We're counting on you, Nymph.

00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:35.417
I'm not really interested in forming a band,

00:07:35.417 --> 00:07:37.958
but I'll stick around, just to pass the time.

00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:40.542
Yeah, by all means!

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.917
The private school folks
are looking for trouble with us

00:07:47.917 --> 00:07:50.000
at this year's culture festival.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.292
In that case, they are looking for
trouble with the Satsukitane Family.

00:07:54.292 --> 00:07:57.125
It's all-out war...

00:07:57.125 --> 00:07:58.958
isn't it?

00:07:59.708 --> 00:08:01.333
"Joint Culture Festival"
"Public vs. Private School"

00:08:01.333 --> 00:08:03.833
<i>And so, at Mikako's behest, </i>

00:08:03.833 --> 00:08:07.125
<i>the Satsukitane private support</i>
<i>squad went into action,</i>

00:08:07.125 --> 00:08:09.792
<i>and demonstrably increased</i>
<i>the size of the audience</i>

00:08:09.792 --> 00:08:12.292
<i>for the Sorami Public School.</i>

00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:14.375
<i>In response to this,</i>
<i>the private school's PTA</i>

00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:17.042
<i>immediately marshaled</i>
<i>their ranks, as well.</i>

00:08:17.042 --> 00:08:18.500
<i>With the power of their money, </i>

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.500
<i>--they conducted large-scale support activities.</i>

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.208
--We're going to win this!
<i>--they conducted large-scale support activities.</i>

00:08:24.542 --> 00:08:28.375
<i>This down-and-dirty rivalry</i>
<i>touched off popular sentiment,</i>

00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:30.750
<i>drawing in the general</i>
<i>population of Sorami.</i>

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.583
To hell with the private school!

00:08:32.583 --> 00:08:35.042
Stick it to 'em, Tomo!

00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:41.667
<i>The music showdown</i>
<i>at the joint culture festival</i>

00:08:41.667 --> 00:08:46.333
<i>divided Sorami in two,</i>
<i>creating an explosive situation.</i>

00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:50.083
<i>Indeed, the whole town</i>
<i>was in a mass-support mood.</i>

00:08:50.083 --> 00:08:53.208
This is really starting to
get serious, Tomo.

00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:55.542
Yikes, we really have to rehearse.

00:08:55.542 --> 00:08:56.917
"Music Room"

00:08:56.917 --> 00:08:59.083
Ikaros, do it again!

00:08:59.083 --> 00:09:02.958
The big night is almost here.
You have to practice harder.

00:09:02.958 --> 00:09:05.417
I am sorry, Master.

00:09:12.417 --> 00:09:14.375
Ikaros...?

00:09:14.375 --> 00:09:15.917
Sohara...

00:09:15.917 --> 00:09:19.458
What's the matter? You look down.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:22.333
I am of no help at all to Master.

00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:24.625
You don't have to worry about that.

00:09:24.625 --> 00:09:27.542
I'm a rank novice on the drums, myself.

00:09:27.542 --> 00:09:28.625
But...

00:09:28.625 --> 00:09:31.083
Awesome! That's perfect, Nymph!

00:09:31.083 --> 00:09:32.792
It's not all that much.

00:09:32.792 --> 00:09:35.667
All right, let's go through it again!

00:09:36.917 --> 00:09:41.542
I know, Ikaros! Why don't
you try one of the other parts?

00:09:41.542 --> 00:09:46.292
There just might be
one that clicks with you.

00:09:46.292 --> 00:09:47.708
Okay.

00:09:53.833 --> 00:09:55.833
W-What the...?

00:10:06.458 --> 00:10:08.750
<i>There's still some time</i>
<i>before we take the stage.</i>

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.208
<i>It is a culture festival--time to enjoy it!</i>

00:10:14.458 --> 00:10:16.375
"Girls Swimming Club"
"Swimsuit Maid Café"

00:10:17.417 --> 00:10:20.083
Welcome to our café, Master.

00:10:20.083 --> 00:10:22.625
W-What are you doing here?

00:10:22.625 --> 00:10:26.042
A friend from class insisted that I do this.

00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:28.083
Ah, Tomo, welcome.

00:10:28.083 --> 00:10:28.750
Sohara!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:32.125
Come on, are you going to order, or not?

00:10:32.125 --> 00:10:33.750
Uh, I'll take a juice.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:34.750
And you?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.417
C-Coffee, please.

00:10:40.417 --> 00:10:41.917
Ah...

00:10:41.917 --> 00:10:43.167
Nice...

00:10:43.167 --> 00:10:46.333
Tomo, we get our break soon.

00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:49.000
Let's look around
the school together, okay?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.125
Yeah, fine...

00:10:51.125 --> 00:10:53.792
So, what can I get you?

00:10:53.792 --> 00:10:55.958
A little more, please.

00:10:55.958 --> 00:10:58.250
A little bit lower...

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:01.042
Tomo, you sicko!

00:11:02.625 --> 00:11:06.917
Things are in full swing, huh?
Where should we go first?

00:11:10.792 --> 00:11:15.708
Look, Tomo, they're doing
a haunted house over there.

00:11:15.708 --> 00:11:17.333
H-Hey!

00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:25.625
What are you doing?

00:11:25.625 --> 00:11:29.875
An exhibition corner. I thought that
I would do a proper presentation

00:11:29.875 --> 00:11:34.000
for the New World Discovery Club,
in addition to the music showdown.

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:39.542
You really want to fly that badly?

00:11:39.542 --> 00:11:43.333
Not everything above
the clouds is good, you know.

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:47.333
I'll bet. Looking at you
and Ikaros, I can tell as much.

00:11:57.375 --> 00:12:00.917
I'm bored. Entertain me.

00:12:00.917 --> 00:12:03.417
W-Well then, shall I sing you a song?

00:12:03.417 --> 00:12:06.625
Or perhaps go and kill all
of the Downers on the ground?

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:10.833
That's no fun. You're useless.
I guess I really will scrap you.

00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:15.750
Please, wait! Anything but that!
I'll do whatever you want!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.667
You've been keeping a pet bird, right?

00:12:19.667 --> 00:12:22.500
Yes. Would you like to see her?

00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:28.458
Even as little as her wings are,

00:12:28.458 --> 00:12:31.333
she apparently wandered
up here to Synapse.

00:12:31.333 --> 00:12:32.917
She has become quite attached to me.

00:12:32.917 --> 00:12:35.083
Pluck them off.

00:12:35.083 --> 00:12:39.625
Hey, don't tell me you're
not going to obey your master.

00:12:39.625 --> 00:12:41.167
No...

00:12:41.167 --> 00:12:43.000
...of course not...

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:59.708
That was quite entertaining.
I'll scrap you some other time.

00:12:59.708 --> 00:13:03.750
Yes, Master. Thank you very much.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:07.833
Thank you... very much...

00:13:11.167 --> 00:13:13.000
Hey, Nymph!

00:13:15.417 --> 00:13:16.833
Here, for you.

00:13:16.833 --> 00:13:17.792
What?

00:13:17.792 --> 00:13:21.417
I promised you, remember?
If I made anything at that shop,

00:13:21.417 --> 00:13:23.417
I'd buy you whatever you liked.

00:13:23.417 --> 00:13:25.292
Oh, that.

00:13:25.292 --> 00:13:28.083
You looked like you
wanted to try a candy apple,

00:13:28.083 --> 00:13:30.250
and you've been doing so well in the band,

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:34.083
so this is to show my appreciation.
Thanks for everything.

00:13:37.708 --> 00:13:43.500
<i>"Thank you." Weren't those</i>
<i>the words that I said?</i>

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.500
Thank you... very much...

00:13:52.542 --> 00:13:56.417
<i>Downers are only beings to look</i>
<i>down on, and trample upon.</i>

00:13:56.417 --> 00:14:00.417
<i>It won't hurt to let them</i>
<i>be nice to me, just a little.</i>

00:14:06.958 --> 00:14:08.125
It's delicious.

00:14:08.125 --> 00:14:09.542
Isn't it?

00:14:14.167 --> 00:14:17.458
Ah, Tomo, you're making Nymph cry!

00:14:17.458 --> 00:14:20.333
Sakurai, you fiend...

00:14:20.333 --> 00:14:22.167
N-No, I...

00:14:25.292 --> 00:14:27.958
What are you doing?

00:14:28.917 --> 00:14:30.458
Nymph...

00:14:30.458 --> 00:14:32.750
...the sky here is wide open.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.375
--Huh? What do you mean? I don't understand.

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:38.167
--Tomo, you've done something else to Nymph, haven't you?!
--Huh? What do you mean? I don't understand.

00:14:38.167 --> 00:14:40.583
I-I didn't do anything!

00:14:41.542 --> 00:14:44.167
I-Is this going to end up being my fault?!

00:14:44.167 --> 00:14:45.750
This candy is yucky.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.750
You said it was delicious a moment ago!

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.792
You hush!

00:14:48.792 --> 00:14:54.208
Now, now, everyone,
calm down. It's almost time.

00:14:54.875 --> 00:14:59.208
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:14:59.958 --> 00:15:01.958
"Shine!! The 42nd Joint
Culture Festival Presentation Hall"

00:15:03.875 --> 00:15:07.250
Private school! Private school!

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:09.167
You show them, Tomo!

00:15:09.167 --> 00:15:11.125
Tomo, <i>banzai</i>!

00:15:11.125 --> 00:15:11.958
Mikako!

00:15:11.958 --> 00:15:14.958
--Young Miss!
--Let them have it!

00:15:14.958 --> 00:15:18.792
And now, on the joint culture
festival main stage,

00:15:18.792 --> 00:15:21.625
we present our music showdown!

00:15:25.167 --> 00:15:27.250
This is a full orchestral concert,

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:31.292
presented by volunteers
from the Sorami Private Academy.

00:15:57.417 --> 00:16:01.333
<i>Well? Eat your heart out, poor people.</i>

00:16:01.333 --> 00:16:05.042
<i>This is what true culture is,</i>
<i>ladies and gentlemen.</i>

00:16:13.167 --> 00:16:15.167
That was perfect!

00:16:16.417 --> 00:16:18.250
Bravo!

00:16:19.542 --> 00:16:22.250
The private school's concert was amazing.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:27.167
Aw, the private school guys
are going to make fools of us again.

00:16:27.167 --> 00:16:32.250
Uh-uh, it's all right. We've got
Sakurai and the others this year!

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.000
Sakurai will take care of this.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.625
Moving on, the New World Discovery Club

00:16:36.625 --> 00:16:39.000
will now present their band concert.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.458
Sakurai! Sakurai!

00:16:42.458 --> 00:16:47.292
Thanks, everyone. Your voices
calling out to me have been heard.

00:16:47.292 --> 00:16:53.042
Performing live is life,
and I'm going to show you my way of life!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:58.292
This song is called
"Tingling Nipples"!

00:17:04.417 --> 00:17:12.625
♪ We're popping out
where it feels good ♪

00:17:12.625 --> 00:17:19.750
♪ We're popping out,
you and us both ♪

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:24.000
♪ It's something that
God decided for us ♪

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:28.917
♪ Tingling, trembling with fear ♪

00:17:28.917 --> 00:17:35.042
♪ Go ahead and touch
me with your gentle hands ♪

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.708
Tomo, this isn't the song that we arranged.

00:17:39.708 --> 00:17:42.417
I'm sorry! I just had to do it!

00:17:45.542 --> 00:17:49.833
Wow, well done.
That was quite entertaining.

00:17:49.833 --> 00:17:53.000
That was a comic band
befitting poor people, huh?

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:56.292
Unfortunately for them,
we've won this handily.

00:17:56.292 --> 00:17:58.083
Now that you've learned your lesson,

00:17:58.083 --> 00:17:59.458
--you poor people should
act like poor people, and...

00:17:59.458 --> 00:18:01.375
--Sorry about that.
--you poor people should act like poor people, and...

00:18:01.375 --> 00:18:05.583
That was just a little side show.

00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:06.417
What?

00:18:06.417 --> 00:18:09.125
Why do they seem so confident?

00:18:16.375 --> 00:18:18.667
The real show starts now.

00:18:20.458 --> 00:18:22.083
Ikaros...

00:18:32.667 --> 00:18:35.375
This song is called "Fallen Down."

00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:40.833
♪ Fallen down ♪

00:18:44.375 --> 00:18:47.792
♪ Blue--an azure sky ♪

00:18:47.792 --> 00:18:51.042
♪ I want to fly through it forever ♪

00:18:51.042 --> 00:18:55.250
♪ but the only one who can fly is you ♪

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:58.417
♪ I can't fly ♪

00:18:58.417 --> 00:19:00.792
♪ The reason being ♪

00:19:00.792 --> 00:19:06.542
♪ that my wings have been tarnished ♪

00:19:06.542 --> 00:19:08.167
♪ Please ♪

00:19:09.542 --> 00:19:13.708
♪ don't leave me here ♪

00:19:13.708 --> 00:19:20.125
♪ For you, I will fly ♪

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:24.083
♪ once again ♪

00:19:24.083 --> 00:19:27.750
♪ The sky is so pretty and blue ♪

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.458
♪ that it brings me to tears ♪

00:19:31.458 --> 00:19:39.417
♪ but I will fly through
it on tarnished wings ♪

00:19:39.417 --> 00:19:46.208
♪ And then, when I get to you, ♪

00:19:46.208 --> 00:19:48.125
♪ that's where I'll fall ♪

00:19:48.125 --> 00:19:50.125
♪ Fallen down ♪

00:19:55.375 --> 00:19:57.667
♪ Fallen down ♪

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:08.500
Ikaros! Ikaros!

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:13.583
Ikaros! Ikaros! Ikaros!

00:20:13.583 --> 00:20:18.750
Ikaros! Ikaros! Ikaros!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:22.042
Ikaros! Ikaros!

00:20:22.042 --> 00:20:25.167
Ikaros! Ikaros!

00:20:26.083 --> 00:20:28.500
Cheers!

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.417
Did you see the look on the
faces of those private school guys?

00:20:31.417 --> 00:20:34.042
Yes. It felt so good.

00:20:34.042 --> 00:20:36.417
It's all thanks to you, Ikaros.

00:20:36.417 --> 00:20:40.208
No, not at all. It was because
everyone performed so well

00:20:40.208 --> 00:20:42.292
that I was able to sing.

00:20:42.292 --> 00:20:48.208
Yeah. Sugata, Chairman,
Nymph and Sohara, you all did great.

00:20:48.208 --> 00:20:49.375
Thanks so much.

00:20:49.375 --> 00:20:50.417
And more than anything,

00:20:50.417 --> 00:20:53.833
my little side show made
the main event stand out so much.

00:20:53.833 --> 00:20:55.833
Oh no it didn't!

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:01.292
By the way, Tomoki,
aren't you going to the afterparty?

00:21:01.292 --> 00:21:02.417
Afterparty?

00:21:02.417 --> 00:21:03.250
Yeah.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.583
The rule is that you have
to go hand-in-hand as couples,

00:21:05.583 --> 00:21:07.333
or they won't let you in.

00:21:07.333 --> 00:21:09.000
It doesn't matter to me.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
--In that case I'll go with...
--Tomo, I'll...

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.417
Um...

00:21:17.708 --> 00:21:20.917
My, my, Sakurai, aren't you popular?

00:21:20.917 --> 00:21:22.333
What?

00:21:25.167 --> 00:21:26.750
Say, Tomo...

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.875
Why don't you take Alpha?

00:21:28.875 --> 00:21:29.667
Why?

00:21:29.667 --> 00:21:33.292
Because Alpha is the one
who did the most this time, right?

00:21:33.292 --> 00:21:37.208
Yeah. Why don't you
take her there, as her reward?

00:21:37.208 --> 00:21:39.042
Right, Ikaros?

00:22:02.292 --> 00:22:12.167
<i>Don't say it's only love</i>

00:22:12.167 --> 00:22:17.542
<i>It's a huge problem for me,</i>

00:22:17.542 --> 00:22:21.042
<i>so complicated </i>

00:22:21.042 --> 00:22:26.292
<i>I'm ready to give up</i>

00:22:26.292 --> 00:22:31.000
<i>figuring out what women think</i>

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:38.917
<i>I'm no match for such intrepid angels</i>

00:22:38.917 --> 00:22:43.542
<i>Your kisses taste like lemon pie</i>

00:22:43.542 --> 00:22:48.292
<i>Your skin smells of lavender</i>

00:22:48.292 --> 00:22:53.042
<i>You turn me on, then turn a cold shoulder</i>

00:22:53.042 --> 00:22:55.458
<i>It torments me</i>

00:22:55.458 --> 00:23:00.000
<i>Couples flit about hither and yon</i>

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.792
<i>with their heads in the clouds </i>

00:23:04.792 --> 00:23:09.500
<i>It stirs me up to no end</i>

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>It's okay, it's okay, just you wait</i>

00:23:35.292 --> 00:23:38.458
<i>Is it right for me to be this happy?</i>

00:23:45.875 --> 00:23:47.708
What's the matter?

00:23:47.708 --> 00:23:48.667
Nothing.

00:23:48.667 --> 00:23:50.625
You're a strange one.

00:23:52.375 --> 00:23:56.917
<i>I am what Master hates...</i>

00:23:56.917 --> 00:23:58.750
<i>a weapon.</i>

00:24:03.583 --> 00:24:08.171
Next time,
"Off We Go To My Bathhouse Paradise"
